    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 72A St Nessans Terrace is an attractive modern semi-detached home, built in 2018 and ideally positioned in a quiet cul-de-sac to the rear of St Peter’s Terrace. Accessed from the top of St Nessans Terrace, the property enjoys a convenient location just above Howth Village, with the village, harbour and an array of local amenities quite literally on your doorstep.\r\n\r\nThe property also benefits from two private off-street car parking spaces, a particularly valuable feature in such a sought-after coastal location.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 79 sq. m. (c. 850 sq. ft.), the well-designed accommodation is bright, contemporary and exceptionally well laid out. The ground floor is entered through a welcoming open porch and opens into a superb open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, creating a generous and versatile space for both everyday living and entertaining. A modern shower room, useful utility area and under-stairs storage complete the accommodation on this level.\r\n\r\nThe living area enjoys a wonderful connection to the outdoors through large sliding patio doors, which open directly onto the south-west facing rear garden. This sunny aspect captures the afternoon and evening sun beautifully, while the extensive glazing allows natural light to flood the interior and creates a bright, inviting atmosphere throughout the home.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, a spacious landing benefits from high ceilings and skylights, adding further light and a sense of space. There are two generously proportioned double bedrooms, together with a further shower room.\r\n\r\nHowth Village, with its excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, pubs, shops and local amenities, is just a few minutes' walk away. The picturesque harbour and the spectacular coastal walks for which the Howth Peninsula is renowned are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nFor commuters, Howth DART Station is approximately a 12-minute walk away, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and beyond.\r\n\r\nBuilt in 2018, the property benefits from modern construction standards and an air-to-water heat pump heating system, together with alu-clad windows, making this an energy-efficient and economical home to run and maintain.\r\n\r\nCombining a superb location, modern accommodation, private parking, a sunny south-west facing garden and excellent energy efficiency, 72A St Nessans Terrace represents an outstanding opportunity to acquire a contemporary home in the heart of Howth.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
